  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (config_006: scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) achieves 0.653 acc, while image-only (resnet50) is very weak at 0.208. The critical unresolved question is whether the image modality provides any complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation, or whether it merely adds noise. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is a minimal extension of our best RNA-only result—adding only the image branch and a simple concat fusion—so it cleanly isolates the effect of multimodal fusion. If it matches or exceeds 0.653, multimodal exploration is justified and we can then test ViT, weighted fusion, or other extensions. If it underperforms, we save budget by ruling out the entire multimodal branch. It is the highest-information experiment because the answer determines the direction of all subsequent experiments, and it changes only one design axis (adding image+fusion) relative to the known best configuration."
}

